Like that's always sort of like, you know, I like it when games do that and they don't fully explain their lore to you.

00:05:54.780 --> 00:05:58.760
So you just have to just have to figure it out yourself for playing the game.

00:05:59.340 --> 00:06:02.100
Right. And this game isn't going to give you any handouts.

00:06:02.260 --> 00:06:05.200
You're pretty much just traveling to different infested bases.

00:06:05.200 --> 00:06:09.280
And your job is to destroy all the aliens on those bases.

00:06:09.500 --> 00:06:11.500
Unless you don't. Right.

00:06:11.720 --> 00:06:12.720
That's totally fine.

00:06:12.840 --> 00:06:18.440
And you'd actually for what it's worth, you know, you could you could just play this game by not playing it.

00:06:18.660 --> 00:06:20.800
You never have to kill anything.

00:06:21.320 --> 00:06:23.600
There's a five minute timer in each stage.

00:06:23.880 --> 00:06:26.120
And when that expires, you just move on.

00:06:26.240 --> 00:06:33.720
But you do get like a report back at the end of each that kind of says, like, from your commander, how how well you did.

00:06:33.880 --> 00:06:40.300
And you get a certain amount of points based on how many aliens you killed and how well you performed.

00:06:40.300 --> 00:06:52.260
Now, we'll get into the actual gameplay for a minute, but it's hard to to not like think of this game as just purely one of those older arcade relic games.

00:06:52.420 --> 00:06:55.120
That's just like a get the high score points.

00:06:55.860 --> 00:06:59.480
Same loop over and over again style game, you know?

00:06:59.620 --> 00:07:01.060
Well, yeah, that's that's what it is.

00:07:01.140 --> 00:07:04.000
There's really no depth to this game.

00:07:04.000 --> 00:07:14.900
It is it's like basically a wave shooter, but there can only be one enemy or one or two enemies on the screen at once.

00:07:16.060 --> 00:07:20.580
There's not really much going in the way of of like power ups.

00:07:20.740 --> 00:07:22.600
I mean, there are some, but we'll get there.

00:07:23.320 --> 00:07:29.440
There's nothing in the way of strategy unless you're trying to do a pacifist run, which is surprisingly easy.

00:07:29.440 --> 00:07:34.740
It's yeah, it's just an arcade game ported to the NES.

00:07:35.540 --> 00:07:43.720
Yeah. And not even ported correctly, though, because the original arcade game was a three player simultaneous game.

00:07:43.720 --> 00:07:48.720
And what was cool about that is that it knew your positions throughout the entirety of the bases.

00:07:49.060 --> 00:07:54.100
So you had the aliens like locked to positions where they were.

00:07:54.160 --> 00:07:56.540
And then it also knew where all three players were.

00:07:56.540 --> 00:08:04.540
So you had this thing where it was actually like, you know, even if it was a small base or small ship or whatever, at least it was alive.

00:08:05.080 --> 00:08:08.960
You know, in the sense of aliens are contaminated in this area.

00:08:09.080 --> 00:08:10.060
I'm going to go here.

00:08:10.240 --> 00:08:11.420
You control this side.

00:08:11.600 --> 00:08:13.500
Like, I think that's interesting as a concept.

00:08:13.500 --> 00:08:14.580
It just didn't happen here.

00:08:14.740 --> 00:08:17.340
I mean, it does do that in a way.

00:08:17.340 --> 00:08:27.240
Like, it does have a I guess the term that you could use for it is it's like a persistent world.

00:08:28.480 --> 00:08:31.660
At least each base, which is what like three or four rooms.

00:08:31.960 --> 00:08:38.320
But so like if you're if both players are in the same room, you'll both show up on that screen.

00:08:38.680 --> 00:08:44.580
But you can also be in other rooms and sort of existing in that same world.

00:08:44.580 --> 00:08:52.080
But it doesn't really matter because all that's happening is it's just spawning just spawning enemies into each room separately.

00:08:53.260 --> 00:08:57.280
I guess it's cool when you cross paths and then you could like take it take them on together.

00:08:57.280 --> 00:09:05.060
But I don't think that there's enough going on on each screen for it to matter as much as it did in the arcade.

00:09:05.060 --> 00:09:08.540
I watched a little bit of footage from the arcade version.

00:09:09.640 --> 00:09:16.380
Yeah. And so, like you said, the aliens just spawn even as you're in the room, like they'll just kind of spawn somewhere within the room.

00:09:16.480 --> 00:09:20.540
And I think that's that's missing the like that.

00:09:20.720 --> 00:09:27.500
What's so cool about the idea of like the base being live and being where everything is, because then you're almost you're not hunting everything down.

00:09:27.500 --> 00:09:29.860
It's just kind of happening and occurring in front of you.

00:09:30.040 --> 00:09:38.360
Yeah. And it'd be so much cooler if like you had to be aware of the doors on either side and then like those doors open and you're not sure if it's going to be your split screen partner.

00:09:38.540 --> 00:09:39.700
Or another alien.

00:09:40.220 --> 00:09:46.240
Instead, it's just like if nothing's in the room, the game will take care of that for you and make sure something enters that room.

00:09:46.480 --> 00:09:54.240
And that almost makes me wonder because I didn't I didn't want to give myself as boring an experience as it would have taken to to do this experiment.

00:09:55.320 --> 00:09:59.360
But I wonder if you even have to move between rooms.

00:09:59.360 --> 00:10:08.260
I know that like only the first couple enemies will drop like a score giving item in each room.

00:10:08.540 --> 00:10:10.000
To, you know, to boost that score up.

00:10:10.160 --> 00:10:15.160
But like, I wonder if you could play this game just standing in the same screen because it just kind of ends.

00:10:15.320 --> 00:10:16.400
It's not like there's any.

00:10:16.980 --> 00:10:20.620
It's not like there's any like end game in each of these bases.

00:10:20.800 --> 00:10:22.520
It just like stops you.

00:10:23.240 --> 00:10:32.060
So I wonder if that's like a timer that would trigger regardless of where you are or if there is some like amount of steps you need to take.

00:10:32.060 --> 00:10:32.960
Like, I don't know.

00:10:33.920 --> 00:10:35.420
Yeah, I think it's a timer, though.

00:10:35.540 --> 00:10:39.280
I think it's just straight like five minutes in in game time.

00:10:39.480 --> 00:10:44.840
Wow. And then that counts as like, all right, on to the next the next base or ship or what have you.

00:10:45.260 --> 00:10:49.420
And what's really strange is you mentioned that there's no ending objective, right?

00:10:49.560 --> 00:10:51.320
Because the aliens just get spawned.

00:10:51.340 --> 00:10:53.660
You kind of have to just like always take them out.

00:10:53.660 --> 00:11:00.680
There's no break period where it's like I can move to the next level earlier because I defeated all the waves or something like that.

00:11:00.840 --> 00:11:01.660
That doesn't happen.

00:11:01.680 --> 00:11:04.400
But also there's just no end to the game either.

00:11:04.640 --> 00:11:05.820
You do the same.

00:11:06.220 --> 00:11:11.740
I think it's eight different, you know, ships, bases, motherships, what have you.

00:11:11.980 --> 00:11:13.000
It's eight of those.

00:11:13.000 --> 00:11:14.100
And then it just repeats.

00:11:14.440 --> 00:11:21.680
And the only thing that would like signify that you've beaten the game is maxing out the score to nine nine nine zero zero zero.

00:11:21.680 --> 00:11:24.620
Yeah, that doesn't sound fun at all.

00:11:24.760 --> 00:11:26.660
I mean, I guess is that that could have been fine.

00:11:27.920 --> 00:11:30.680
Like, again, I'm looking rampage.

00:11:30.800 --> 00:11:33.060
I was talking about, like, I don't really care if it's open ended.

00:11:33.200 --> 00:11:35.360
I just like to do the thing in the game.

00:11:37.860 --> 00:11:49.160
But the game here is like the stiffest gunplay, almost zero sound design for enemies tops.

00:11:49.160 --> 00:11:52.100
Half the screen is your action.

00:11:53.620 --> 00:11:59.100
I can't really think of other than the want to beat a game.

00:11:59.560 --> 00:12:03.580
What would keep me playing for longer than the amount of time I did for this podcast?

00:12:04.200 --> 00:12:07.940
And that's why it needs for especially for a console version.

00:12:08.180 --> 00:12:11.980
Right. And I know we're early into consoles making a resurgence.

00:12:11.980 --> 00:12:16.500
We really only have at this point the NES and the master system at home anyway.

00:12:17.100 --> 00:12:20.740
But and maybe some computer consoles if people are like into that scene.

00:12:20.860 --> 00:12:21.800
That's really all you have.

00:12:21.920 --> 00:12:23.060
So we were early in on that.

00:12:23.160 --> 00:12:31.120
But I feel like console gaming needs to offer something in the form of a beginning and end for not even like a campaign.

00:12:31.120 --> 00:12:40.200
But in the sense of like, imagine if this game actually had an ending after the eighth stage.

00:12:40.360 --> 00:12:43.680
Right. And then you saw the ending or whatever.

00:12:43.860 --> 00:12:46.100
And then you could keep playing for high score.

00:12:46.160 --> 00:12:53.660
But this way, there's actually like a motivation of like, you know, you've cleared this galaxy and then you move on to another galaxy or something.

00:12:53.660 --> 00:13:06.480
You know, like it needs a reason to end because like you said, unless you're going for points, there's no reason to keep playing because the gameplay itself will not change at all from the first level.

00:13:06.700 --> 00:13:13.080
Other than adding some new enemies, some new floors, like, you know, the number of rooms in a base.

00:13:13.080 --> 00:13:22.640
And I mean, like, honestly, maybe the difficulty ramps up, but, you know, not not like considerably enough to keep a player engaged.

00:13:23.120 --> 00:13:32.740
Yeah. And it's like there's no late game gear that'd be like, oh, I can't wait for like right now.

00:13:32.940 --> 00:13:39.200
It's just kind of tedious, but I'll get that power trip once I get the BFG or something like that.

00:13:39.200 --> 00:13:46.600
Like this game handles power ups in such a weird way that you can find grenades lying around.

00:13:46.760 --> 00:13:49.600
And I think it's like down in a or something to throw a grenade.

00:13:49.640 --> 00:13:51.640
But there's no counter.

00:13:51.820 --> 00:13:54.460
So it's not like you can do any resource management with that.

00:13:54.600 --> 00:13:56.680
It's just sort of like you either have them or you don't.

00:13:57.260 --> 00:14:03.400
I guess there's a like a more there's like a rapid fire pistol.

00:14:04.540 --> 00:14:06.420
But I'd never got that drop.

00:14:07.900 --> 00:14:10.580
So then I guess I got the rapid fire pistol and I liked it.

00:14:10.640 --> 00:14:14.340
I like that rapid fire pistol because that actually like.

00:14:15.200 --> 00:14:21.500
Well, you know, OK, so look, when you're fighting the aliens, right, which is a weird thing to say because you're barely fighting them.

00:14:21.640 --> 00:14:28.860
Yeah, there's this there's this moment where you realize all you have other than these grenades, if you stumble upon them, you just have your gun.

00:14:28.860 --> 00:14:34.740
So you shoot at the alien and it just kind of like one type of alien.

00:14:34.960 --> 00:14:39.360
It is it either lunges at you or just shoots at you from a distance or comes closer to you.

00:14:39.580 --> 00:14:42.660
There's not really a lot of options in terms of defense for you.

00:14:42.800 --> 00:14:43.780
There is a jump.

00:14:43.780 --> 00:14:55.140
But if there's two aliens in a room, most likely based on the jump that they've provided you with and the inputs that it requires, you are most likely just going to jump into the other alien enemy or what have you.

00:14:55.300 --> 00:15:00.100
You know, like and that sounds bad because there's it's pretty much impossible to dodge.

00:15:00.260 --> 00:15:06.560
And if you do dodge, it's like it doesn't feel that good to be dodging it because now you just have to go back to shooting until it lunges back at you the other way.

00:15:07.100 --> 00:15:10.460
However, you have a ton of health in this game.

00:15:10.940 --> 00:15:14.040
So it's almost like inconsequential when you get hit by an alien.

00:15:14.220 --> 00:15:19.860
It's almost like, all right, well, I'd rather get hit than take the effort to dodge and just keep shooting at him.

00:15:19.960 --> 00:15:23.120
And be floating in midair for like a second and a half.

00:15:23.300 --> 00:15:28.900
Exactly. And some enemies do take a lot of bullets to to die.

00:15:29.100 --> 00:15:32.520
So it's almost like a waste of time to be jumping around and dodging.

00:15:32.520 --> 00:15:38.640
It's like, just take the 10 or so points that it knocks off your health because you have a thousand health or something like that.

00:15:38.700 --> 00:15:45.420
And you do get health regeneration, too, through power ups, which is a pretty frequent power up you'll you'll come across.

00:15:45.780 --> 00:15:52.220
So I don't really see a reason to be afraid of the aliens if if they give you that much help.

00:15:52.620 --> 00:16:01.180
There was also another there was another little aspect to fighting in this game that was unique.

00:16:01.180 --> 00:16:12.280
I thought, but it was the only unique thing or it was like it would have been a cool feature if the fighting in this game had any other depth to it.

00:16:12.420 --> 00:16:18.140
But it was basically like if you get lunged at, there's like a chance that you're going to get knocked over.

00:16:18.680 --> 00:16:26.460
You can still shoot from lying on your back and you're going to be right in line with whatever put you there.

00:16:27.620 --> 00:16:32.240
But you can't move until you press the jump button to stand back up.

00:16:32.400 --> 00:16:39.740
I thought that that was interesting because it in in some other version of this game, it could have been like an interesting risk reward.

00:16:39.740 --> 00:16:51.680
If you want to just stay prone and get some shots in and just like finish off the alien or you could get up and try and reposition to a safer area.

00:16:52.100 --> 00:17:01.040
But since there wasn't really much at stake there, like it that that part of this game really didn't mean anything to you.

00:17:01.100 --> 00:17:03.440
Did you did you notice that about like when you get knocked over?

00:17:03.440 --> 00:17:05.000
Yeah, no, it's really cool.

00:17:05.000 --> 00:17:08.940
And it's a level of thought that they didn't put into most of the rest of the game.

00:17:09.080 --> 00:17:13.640
